<h1 class="fs-37 lh-37 mb-24">Layouts</h1>
<p class="mb-32">Use these structures to arrange your content, then replace the images and copy with your own. Each example includes a live preview and matching HTML.</p>
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Image left, text right</h2>
<p class="mb-24">A fifty-fifty layout with an image beside a vertically centered heading and paragraph. <code>flex-md</code> enables flex from 820 pixels, <code>flex-1</code> shares the available width between columns, and <code>items-center</code> handles vertical alignment. Below medium, the image appears above the text.</p>
{% set left %}{% include "components/layouts/image-left.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(left, "Image left, text right") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Text left, image right</h2>
<p class="mb-24">The same structure with the content order swapped. Below medium, the heading and paragraph appear before the image. Both examples preserve their HTML reading order.</p>
{% set right %}{% include "components/layouts/image-right.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(right, "Text left, image right") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Three column</h2>
<p class="mb-24">A section heading followed by three existing vertical cards. <code>flex-md</code> switches the parent to flex from 820 pixels, and <code>flex-1</code> on each wrapper shares the available row width equally. Below medium the cards stack. <code>gap-24</code> separates columns, and <code>mb-24</code> separates stacked cards.</p>
{% set three %}{% include "components/layouts/three-column.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(three, "Three column") }}
<p class="mb-24">The cards reuse the existing sample content and its 344-pixel width cap. Replace the sample links when adapting the layout; the sample blog post is not included in this site.</p>
<p>Replace the static placeholders with your own images, updating their alternative text and dimensions. Layout section headings use <code>h2</code>; the cards retain their <code>h3</code> headings.</p>
<p><a href="/docs/flexbox/">Flexbox utilities</a> · <a href="/docs/images/">Image utilities</a></p>
</article>
